NpuEmbeddings -- mppose (MediaPipe person det + pose landmarks) on the CPU
  model      mediapipe-pose: detector 224px, landmarks 256px, 2254 anchors over 3 levels, 39 rows of 5 (of which 33 are keypoints)
  rotation   between the detector's keypoints 0 (mid-hip) and 1 (full body), both read from the container; the RoI is the square on the hip whose half-side is that distance
  thresholds score 0.500, nms IoU 0.300, top_k 5000, pose conf 0.500, box enlarge 1.00 then 1.25 -- from the container, not a flag
  normalise  detector (x/255 - 0.5)/0.5, border 0.0 in TENSOR space; landmarks (x/255 - 0.0)/1.0, border 0.0 in the raster
  ops        (npu = dispatched, host = this process)
             45 x conv + 28 x dwconv    host  person detector, 93 nodes; dwconv has no [M,N] GEMM to dispatch, so it would not move even with a design set
             54 x conv + 34 x dwconv    host  landmark network, 120 nodes, once per person
             add, maxpool, resize       host  elementwise and memory passes
             d2s (DepthToSpace)         host  this architecture's own op: three of them build the detector's 28/14/7 pyramid out of one 7x7 map, DCR order
             image front end            host  bilinear letterbox to 224px, normalise in float and pad with 0 in TENSOR space; per person a rotated INTER_AREA crop to 256px
             threshold, nms, inverse letterbox host  host-side by construction: a list of survivors, not a tensor
